---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Portfolio"
  description="Regime-conditional strategic weight distributions per risk profile, with a templated conditional implication and the engine states each weight was built from — read live from the FinDynamics API. Distributions, never targets; no trade commands."
  eyebrow="FinDynamics"
  heading="Strategic weights, as a distribution"
  intro="Not a target and not a trade. For each risk profile the portfolio layer tilts a neutral strategic mix by the engines' confidence-weighted, risk-adjusted expected returns, and reports the result as a distribution — a fan whose width is how confident the engines are. A missing or stale engine falls back to its neutral weight and the whole allocation is flagged degraded."
>
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="profile-h">
    <div class="panel__head">
      <h2 id="profile-h">Risk profile</h2>
      <span class="panel__note">/api/v1/portfolio?profile=</span>
    </div>
    <p class="prose">
      Three profiles, least to most risk-seeking. The switcher re-reads the API; every weight
      below is the median of a distribution, and the box and whiskers are its spread.
    </p>
    <div id="portfolio-switcher" class="switcher" role="group" aria-label="Risk profile"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="weights-h">
    <div class="panel__head">
      <h2 id="weights-h">Weight distribution</h2>
      <span class="panel__note">quantiles per asset</span>
    </div>
    <p class="prose">
      One row per asset. The box spans the 25th–75th percentile of the weight, the whiskers the
      5th–95th, the marker is the median, and the hollow tick is the profile's neutral weight —
      so the tilt is the distance between them. A degraded asset collapses to a point at neutral.
    </p>
    <div id="portfolio-weights" style="margin-top:0.85rem"></div>
    <div id="portfolio-legend" style="margin-top:0.5rem"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="implication-h">
    <div class="panel__head">
      <h2 id="implication-h">Conditional implication</h2>
      <span class="panel__note">FINDYN_V1_SPEC.md &sect;12</span>
    </div>
    <p class="prose">
      Reviewed text, templated from the tilt — not model-generated, and conditional throughout.
      It is an implication of the distribution, not an instruction.
    </p>
    <div id="portfolio-implication" style="margin-top:0.5rem"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="why-h">
    <div class="panel__head">
      <h2 id="why-h">Why these weights</h2>
      <span class="panel__note">input AssetState references</span>
    </div>
    <p class="prose">
      Every allocation is only as good as the engine states behind it. This lists each input
      <code>AssetState</code> — its regime, expected return, risk and confidence, and whether it
      was fresh — so a weight can be traced back to the engine that moved it.
    </p>
    <div id="portfolio-why" style="margin-top:0.85rem"></div>
  </section>
</Base>

<script>
  import '../scripts/portfolio';
</script>
